===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|seventy}}, {{m|enm|sevynty}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hundseofontiġ}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sebuntēhundą|t=seventy}}, equivalent to {{af|en|seven|-ty}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|seiventy|t=seventy}}, {{cog|stq|soogentich|t=seventy}}, {{cog|fy|santich|t=seventy}}, {{cog|nl|zeventig|t=seventy}}, {{cog|nds-de|söventig|t=seventy}}, {{cog|de|siebzig|t=seventy}}, {{cog|sv|sjuttio|t=seventy}}, {{cog|no|sytti|t=seventy}}, {{cog|is|sjötíu|t=seventy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛv.ən.ti/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛv.ən.di/|a=US, also}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-seventy.ogg|a=US}}

===Numeral===
{{head|en|numeral}}

# The cardinal number occurring after [[sixty-nine]] and before [[seventy-one]], represented in Roman numerals as [[LXX]] and in Arabic numerals as 70.

